Uniformly for all $\lambda'\le\lambda$, $$\label{eq:smoothed-mass}
\|S_rP'\|_2\le Cr^{-1},$$ and, writing $d=d_g(x,y)$, $$\begin{aligned}
\left\langle S_rP,*S_rP'\right\rangle_{L^2}
&\ge cr^{-4}\iint_{d<r}
|\ell-\tau_{yx}m|^2\,d\lambda(x,\ell)\,d\lambda'(y,m)
\nonumber\\
&\quad-Cr^{-2}\iint(1+d/r)^{-6}\,d\mu(x)\,d\mu'(y).
\label{eq:positive-pairing}
\end{aligned}$$ Moreover $$\label{eq:shell}
r^{-2}\int_X(1+d_g(x,y)/r)^{-6}\,d\mu(x)\le C.$$

The correction $Q$ belongs to $L^2$, and $$\label{eq:angular}
\mathcal I_r:=
\iint_{d_g(x,y)<r}|\ell-\tau_{yx}m|^2
\,d\lambda(x,\ell)\,d\lambda(y,m)\le Cr^4.$$ For every positive current $P'$ represented by $\lambda'\le\lambda$, $$\label{eq:cross-vanish}
\lim_{r\downarrow0}\left\langle S_rP',*S_rQ\right\rangle_{L^2}=0.$$

Fix a smooth almost complex structure $J$ and a $J$-Hermitian metric on a closed four-manifold. Suppose that $$P(\alpha)=\int_{\mathscr C}\alpha_x(\ell)\,d\lambda(x,\ell)$$ for a finite positive measure $\lambda$, with projection $\mu$. Suppose also that $Q\in L^2$ is anti-invariant and that $P+Q$ is a closed current. Assume the estimates $$\begin{aligned}
\mu(B_r(x))&\le Cr^2,\label{eq:abstract-growth}\\
\iint_{d_g(x,y)<r}|\ell-\tau_{yx}m|^2
\,d\lambda(x,\ell)\,d\lambda(y,m)&\le Cr^4
\label{eq:abstract-angular}
\end{aligned}$$ for all sufficiently small $r$, uniformly in $x$.

Under the hypotheses of Theorem <a href="#thm:splitting" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="thm:splitting">13</a>, $$\label{eq:transverse}
\mathcal N_r:=
\int_{\mathscr C}\int_{B_r(x)}
\left|\operatorname{pr}_{L_\ell^\perp}\frac{z_x(y)}r\right|^2
\,d\mu(y)\,d\lambda(x,\ell)=o(r^2).$$

